{"name":"Mediterranean","hex":"#60797d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Mediterranean","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of or pertaining to the Mediterranean Sea and its surrounding region."]},{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["Ellipsis of the Mediterranean Sea: a sea between Europe and Africa, an inland branch of the Atlantic.","A region of Southern Europe and North Africa and West Asia. The region surrounding the Mediterranean Sea."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Mediterranean"}],"entries":[{"title":"Mediterranean Sea","blocks":[{"text":"The Mediterranean Sea is an intercontinental sea situated between Europe, Asia, and Africa. It is surrounded by the Mediterranean basin and almost completely enclosed by land: on the east by the Levant in West Asia, on the north by Anatolia in West Asia and Southern Europe, and on the south by North Africa. To its west it is connected to the Atlantic Ocean via the Strait of Gibraltar that separates the Iberian Peninsula in Europe from Morocco in Africa by only 14 km (9 mi); additionally, it is connected to the Black Sea through the Bosporus strait that intersects Turkey in the northeast and the Red Sea via the Suez Canal in the southeast."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Mediterranean_Sea_16.61811E_38.99124N.jpg/330px-Mediterranean_Sea_16.61811E_38.99124N.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mediterranean_Sea","wikidata":"Q4918"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Greece_Orbit_Photo_1989_by_Atlas_STS-34.jpg/500px-Greece_Orbit_Photo_1989_by_Atlas_STS-34.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Greece_Orbit_Photo_1989_by_Atlas_STS-34.jpg/1280px-Greece_Orbit_Photo_1989_by_Atlas_STS-34.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign